      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "Verified every field of this section line by line against the current official text of 247 CMR 10.00 (mass.gov PDF dated 04/25/2025, effective 1/9/25), 247 CMR 11.00, 247 CMR 7.00, 247 CMR 2.00, M.G.L. c. 94C, s. 7(a), M.G.L. c. 112, s. 61 and M.G.L. c. 12, s. 11I 1/2. The six credentials named in 247 CMR 10.01 are reproduced exactly and the individual/entity split is right; the section correctly notes that the pharmacy intern is NOT in the 247 CMR 10.01 list but IS named in 247 CMR 10.03(1)(f). The chapeau of 10.03(1), the five practice grounds (f) through (i) and (m), the three limbs of (q), the out-of-state ground (t), the 10.06(7) proviso, the 10.03(2) preservation of adjudication-made grounds and the 10.03(3) carve-out with its two conjunctive qualifiers all match the promulgated words, including the placement of 'without cause' in the first limb of (q) only and the 'legally entitled' element in the third. The 247 CMR 10.02 definition of conviction, and its second sentence making a conviction conclusive evidence of commission in a proceeding based upon it, are reproduced accurately. The entity-holder claims are supported: 247 CMR 11.01(1) issues a Board controlled substance registration to a pharmacy, outsourcing facility or wholesale drug business, 247 CMR 11.03 requires the applicant to be qualified for a pharmacy license, outsourcing facility registration or wholesale druggist license first, and M.G.L. c. 94C, s. 7(a) sends every other registrant to the commissioner of public health while sending wholesale druggists, outsourcing facilities and pharmacies to this Board. Absolute words ('only', 'no', 'nothing') were checked one by one and each is carried by the regulatory text. The section declares periods, sanctions and the enumerated M.G.L. c. 112, s. 61 grounds outside its scope and does not stray into them. All six listed practice questions (MA-Q-0262, 0264, 0267, 0268, 0270, 0272) are answerable from the section and none is contradicted by it. Nothing wrong found; publishable as it stands."
