      "summary": "Verified every field of this section against the current official text of 247 CMR 10.00 (mass.gov PDF dated 04/25/2025, effective 1/9/25), 247 CMR 4.02, 247 CMR 2.00, M.G.L. c. 30A, s. 13 and M.G.L. c. 112, s. 61. The 247 CMR 10.02 definitions of Complaint, Investigative Conference, Adjudicatory Hearing and Order to Show Cause are reproduced accurately, and the teaching that the conference is an alternative rather than a mandatory gateway is exactly what 247 CMR 10.04 and 10.05 say. The 10.06 classification is correct in every cell: the advisory letter does not constitute formal disciplinary action, a reprimand does and a censure is a severe reprimand, probation constitutes discipline but permits practice under Board conditions, and 10.06(3) attaches no practice restriction to a reprimand or censure. Every period was checked against the text and against what it is counted from: seven days under 10.07 from the Board's action, 15 business days under 10.08(3) from the Board's or Board President's action, seven business days under 10.03(1)(y) and (z), 30 days in writing under 10.03(1)(aa). The section correctly attributes the word 'non-disciplinary' to 247 CMR 10.08(1) rather than to 10.06(8) and (9), and correctly preserves the Board's separate 247 CMR 10.07 power to suspend or refuse to renew before any hearing on the merits notwithstanding the 10.06(5) formula - a point also supported by M.G.L. c. 30A, s. 13, whose definition of 'License' covers a registration and which expressly contemplates suspension without a prior hearing. The four voluntary surrender requirements in 10.06(6)(a) through (d), including the statement that the surrender is not subject to judicial review, are reproduced exactly, as is the reading that 'permanent or for a fixed period of time' attaches to the surrender and not to the voluntary suspension beside it. 247 CMR 4.02(6) and (7) were read word for word: the repeated 'has been' in (6) does keep the six-months-to-two-years band on the suspension limb, the MPJE is required in both tiers, and the NAPLEX appears only in (7) and only among the conditions the Board may determine. All eight listed practice questions (MA-Q-0211, 0223, 0255, 0263, 0265, 0266, 0269, 0271) are answerable from the section and none is contradicted by it; in particular MA-Q-0255 correctly excludes the NAPLEX for a nine-month suspension, which the section teaches. One Low-severity shorthand was recorded: a single table cell says renewal after 'suspension or revocation' is governed by 247 CMR 4.02(6) or (7) without repeating the two qualifiers the section states correctly in at least six other places (that 4.02 governs personal registration renewal, and that neither tier reaches a suspension shorter than six months). That imprecision does not mislead a candidate reading the section as a whole, so every criterion passes and the section is publishable as it stands."
